# Optional overrides for vps-docker-clean.service.
# Install manually as /etc/default/vps-docker-clean if needed.
# This is a systemd EnvironmentFile, not a shell script.
# DOCKER must be an executable name or path, not a command line with arguments.
# Do not use shell expansions or append command arguments here.
# *_UNTIL values must be positive whole hours, for example 24h or 168h.
# They measure creation age, not how long a container has been stopped.
# The managed .policy file supplies defaults; this file overrides runtime ages.
# Change profile/cache budget through install.sh --profile / --cache-gib.
# Native cache GC requires Docker Engine 28+. Old cache overrides are rejected.

# DOCKER=docker
# CONTAINER_UNTIL=48h
# NETWORK_UNTIL=72h
# IMAGE_UNTIL=168h

# 0 disables pressure; set a host-specific free-space floor.
# IMAGE_MIN_FREE_GIB=5
# Choose additional image protection; container source IDs are always retained.
# inventory (default): deployment publishes the strict digest inventory.
# none: no additional images are protected; no inventory is needed.
# tags: keep the local image IDs for the exact tags in IMAGE_KEEP_TAGS.
# IMAGE_PROTECTION_MODE=inventory
# For tags mode, supply whitespace-separated repository:tag names that appear
# exactly in local Docker image RepoTags; latest is an ordinary literal tag.
# IMAGE_PROTECTION_MODE=tags
# IMAGE_KEEP_TAGS="example.test/app:latest example.test/app:rollback"
# Leave IMAGE_KEEP_TAGS unset or empty in none/inventory mode.
# IMAGE_PROTECTION_FILE=/etc/default/vps-docker-clean.images.json
# All modes use IMAGE_PROTECTION_FILE plus .lock for cleanup/deployment locking.
# Only inventory mode reads the inventory itself; see README.
